videos.script:
There are more roads to a phone than the two this course has taken, and today you look at three of them. {{three}}

Lesson 1 asked who draws the screen. A WebView, for Capacitor. The platform's own views, for React Native. And there is a third answer. {{third}} Flutter paints every pixel itself, like a game.

You will build the planner in Flutter, and the rules have to be written again, in Dart. {{dart}} Then you will see what a screen reader gets from a page that is one big picture: a single button, and nothing else, until Flutter turns on a tree of its own. {{semantics}}

Then Ionic, phone controls for the web, which Capacitor wraps like anything else. {{ionic}} And NativeScript, which reaches the platform's interfaces straight from TypeScript.

Last, a way to choose. {{choose}} For a web team, it is mostly how much of what you have comes along.
